		"outcome": {"first": "Isolde stood at the window for a long time. 'One,' she said. 'It is all I asked. It is a great deal.' She took the third cup down from its hook, and set it, carefully, beside the others, and for the first time in your hearing she sat, and let the tower keep its own lamp.",
			"all": "'All nineteen.' Isolde read her plan over twice with her finger on the ruled lines, and then she laughed, helplessly, and put her hand to her face. 'Exactly as drawn. I never thought it would be exactly as drawn. I thought something would go wrong.'",
